{% comment %}
  Step 6 — post-booking success screen, shown after "Confirm payment" is
  tapped on the Confirmation step. No progress dots and no back button
  here on purpose (matches the Figma reference) — booking is done, there's
  nothing to go back to.

  MOBILE REDESIGN per a later Figma pass (node 438:7571), same instruction
  as the previous five steps: stay with the design, ignore backend
  integration.
  - Added the same shared kal-booking-flow-appointment-card.liquid used
    on Slot Picker/Patient Details, right below the intro — this screen
    didn't have one before.
  - "Reference No." row removed — not in the export. "Day & Time" renamed
    to "Date & Time" to match it.
  - "Payment" row is now dynamic (data-kal-confirm-payment), reflecting
    whichever card was selected on Confirmation's new Payment Method
    section ("Online payment" / "Pay at clinic") instead of the old
    always-"At the Clinic" text — see setPaymentMethod() in
    kal-booking-flow.js, which now also updates this alongside toggling
    the selected card.
  - "Before your visit" restyled from a bordered, inset card to a
    full-bleed tinted band (edge-to-edge, top/bottom border only, no
    corner radius) to match the export.

  CARD REDESIGN, later Figma pass (node 656:5433) — replaces the
  appointment-card + Consultation Details list above with one bordered
  "confirmed card" (.kal-confirmed-card) combining a date badge, the
  time/mode/relative-eta line, a dashed divider with the export's
  cutout-circle notches, a doctor row, and a Patient/Payment two-cell
  grid. Originally In-Clinic only (data-kal-mode-offline-only), with
  Video Consult keeping the older appointment-card + Consultation
  Details layout (no online-mode spec had been given for that pass) —
  per explicit instruction, this card is now shown for BOTH modes and
  that older layout is gone entirely. Mode/Patient reuse the exact same
  data-kal-confirm-mode/-name hooks renderConfirmationSummary() in
  kal-booking-flow.js already populates per mode, so no JS changes were
  needed; Payment stays the same static "₹450 Paid" mockup regardless of
  mode, same as this card already showed for In-Clinic.
  - "Booking ID AYR-20486" chip, new — added under the intro subtext, same
    generic addition regardless of mode.
  - Date badge (FRI/06/AUG), the "10:30 AM" time, and the "in 3 days"
    relative-eta chip are static mockup values straight from the export —
    same category as the doctor's photo/fee placeholders elsewhere in
    this flow, no hook exists (or is worth adding) to derive a day-badge
    + relative-day string from slotPicker's state for a screen this
    build isn't wiring to the backend anyway.
  - Mode/duration text reuses the existing data-kal-confirm-mode hook
    as-is (renderConfirmationSummary() in kal-booking-flow.js already
    populates it as "In Clinic - 30 mins") rather than introduce a
    second, differently-formatted mode hook just to match the export's
    exact "In-clinic, 30 mins" punctuation.
  - Patient cell reuses data-kal-confirm-name, same hook Confirmation's
    own details list already uses.
  - Payment cell is a static "₹450 Paid" per the export, NOT the old
    data-kal-confirm-payment text hook (which produced a plain "Online
    payment"/"Pay at clinic" string, not a price + paid badge) — now
    that the old per-mode appointment-card + Consultation Details layout
    is gone entirely, that hook has no matching element anywhere in this
    file; setPaymentMethod()'s querySelectorAll() over it no-ops
    harmlessly.
  - "Before your visit" band recolored from the mint tint to the export's
    sand/tan treatment (background, label, and icon-tint colors) and its
    check icons moved into their own white rounded-8 boxes; copy trimmed
    to the export's three items (arrival, ID + referral, reports) — the
    old "pay at reception" item is gone since payment is already settled
    per the new card above.
  - "Back to Homepage" button, new — a footer this step never had before,
    using the same shared .kal-step-doctor-select__continue treatment as
    every other step's primary CTA. Static mockup like the rest of this
    build — points at the shop's root URL, no click handler needed.

  Patient Name, Mode, and Date & Time reuse the EXACT SAME data-kal-confirm-*
  hooks as the Confirmation (review) step — renderConfirmationSummary() in
  kal-booking-flow.js already does flow.querySelectorAll() for each of
  those, so this step's matching elements get populated for free with zero
  JS changes.

  "Reschedule or cancel" (data-kal-reschedule-cancel) is now removed —
  explicit instruction, confirming it's genuinely absent from this
  screen's design rather than just scrolled out of the earlier export.
  It had no click handler wired up anyway (that's a separate,
  already-designed feature — localStorage token + minimal-info lookup —
  documented elsewhere, not part of this screen's build), so nothing else
  depended on it.

  The Confirmation step's "Confirm payment" button now also carries
  data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed" (alongside its existing
  data-kal-confirm-booking hook) so the full flow is clickable through to
  this screen for demo purposes, even though nothing is actually booked
  yet on the backend.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — consolidated
  into the shared step shell (see "SHARED STEP SHELL" in
  kal-booking-flow.css), same correction as the Confirmation step: the
  success icon, intro, and full Consultation Details card were
  byte-for-byte identical between the old mobile and desktop blocks. No
  progress-dots/back-button on this step at any width (booking is done,
  nothing to navigate back to), so unlike the other consolidated steps
  there's no .kal-step-shell__header here — just a bare close button in
  the corner (.kal-step-booking-confirmed__header), same treatment as
  Therapy Confirmed's own __header: absolutely positioned rather than a
  normal-flow row, so it doesn't reserve height above .kal-step-shell__scroll
  and unbalance that region's justify-content:center (see
  kal-booking-flow.css's comment on that rule).
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed kal-step-shell">

  {%- comment -%}
    Moved OUT of .kal-step-shell__panel to be a direct child of this
    outer element instead, same reason .kal-step-booking-confirmed__hero
    below it was pulled out — absolute positioning anchors to the
    nearest POSITIONED ancestor, not to DOM nesting depth, so this only
    needs .kal-step-booking-confirmed itself to be position:relative
    (see CSS). Previously this stayed nested in .kal-step-shell__panel,
    which worked fine when hero was ALSO inside the panel (its own
    negative margin-bottom pulled the card below it up, not the panel
    itself) — but now that hero is a panel sibling for CSS Grid
    placement, that same negative margin pulls the whole panel up
    instead, so a header still anchored to the panel landed near the
    appointment card instead of the dialog's top-right corner on Video
    Consult's single-column layout. Anchoring to the outer element (which
    wraps hero + panel in both the single-column and two-column In-Clinic
    layouts) keeps this pinned to the true top-right corner in both.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed__header">
    <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-close aria-label="Close">
      {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'close' -%}
    </button>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    In-Clinic desktop only (node "Frame 3940") — repurposes this step's
    own left info column (previously dead markup: .kal-step-shell__info
    is display:none at every width by the rule further down, so this
    "You're all set"/location content never actually rendered). Just the
    "Need assistance?" line (reusing .kal-step-entry__help, the same one
    every other step's desktop footer uses) — no separate copy of the
    success icon/heading/subtext here. .kal-step-booking-confirmed__hero
    below is the ONE copy of that content that exists in this file;
    kal-booking-flow.css repositions that SAME element into this column
    via CSS Grid placement (grid-column/grid-row, gated by a :has() on
    this element's own data-kal-mode-offline-only [hidden] state) rather
    than duplicating it here and hiding one copy — see the CSS's own
    comment on why grid-row placement (not just grid-column) is what
    lets these two stack correctly within the one column.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info kal-step-booking-confirmed__info" data-kal-mode-offline-only>
    <div class="kal-step-entry__help">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--help">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'help-circle' -%}
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__help-text">Need assistance? Call us at +91 804012 3456</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Mint hero band behind the success icon/heading — the export's own
    markup has this section overlap 24px behind the card below it
    (mb-[-24px] in the export) on mobile/Video Consult desktop, so the
    band's bottom edge tucks under the card's rounded top corners
    instead of stopping flush above it. A direct .kal-step-booking-confirmed
    child (not nested inside .kal-step-shell__panel) specifically so
    CSS Grid can place it in the LEFT column on desktop for In-Clinic
    (see kal-booking-flow.css) — grid item placement only works on
    direct children of the grid container, and this is the one copy of
    this content in the file (no duplicate + hide-one-copy).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed__hero">
    <div class="kal-confirmation-success-icon">
      <span class="kal-confirmation-success-icon__inner">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed__intro">
      <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Appointment confirmed</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__subtext">A confirmation is sent to your WhatsApp number.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      {%- comment -%}
          Replaces the old ticket/notch .kal-confirmed-card entirely
          (explicit instruction — remove it) — this is now the one card
          shown for both modes at every width, the exact same
          .kal-confirmation-appointment-card the Confirmation step's own
          review card uses (photo/eyebrow/name header, then Mode/Date &
          Time/Patient/Payment rows). Mode/Date & Time/Patient reuse the
          same data-kal-confirm-*/data-kal-doctor-* hooks
          renderConfirmationSummary()/applySelectedDoctorToCards() in
          kal-booking-flow.js already populate — zero JS changes needed.
          Payment reads "Paid online" for Video Consult or "Pay at
          clinic" for In-Clinic — same data-kal-mode-online-only/
          -offline-only toggle the Mode row's own icon swap above already
          uses (applyConsultationModeVisibility() in kal-booking-flow.js
          is generic over any element carrying those attributes, so this
          needed no JS changes). Was a single static "Paid online" string
          regardless of mode, which read wrong for In-Clinic bookings
          (nothing here is actually paid online once you can pay at the
          clinic instead).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card">
          <div class="kal-appointment-card kal-confirmation-appointment-card__top">
            <span class="kal-appointment-card__photo kal-appointment-card__photo--placeholder" data-kal-doctor-photo-display></span>
            <span class="kal-appointment-card__body">
              <span class="kal-appointment-card__eyebrow">Consultation</span>
              <span class="kal-appointment-card__name" data-kal-doctor-name-display>Dr. Neethu Jayachandran</span>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__rows">
            <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
              <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
                <span data-kal-mode-online-only hidden>{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'mode-online' -%}</span>
                <span data-kal-mode-offline-only>{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'mode-location' -%}</span>
                Mode
              </span>
              <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-mode>&mdash;</span>
            </div>
            <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
              <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
                {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'calendar-days' -%}
                Date &amp; Time
              </span>
              <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-datetime>&mdash;</span>
            </div>
            <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
              <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
                {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'user' -%}
                Patient
              </span>
              <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-name>&mdash;</span>
            </div>
            <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
              <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
                {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'credit-card' -%}
                Payment
              </span>
              <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value kal-confirmation-details__value--paid">
                <span data-kal-mode-online-only hidden>Paid online</span>
                <span data-kal-mode-offline-only>Pay at clinic</span>
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        "Before your visit" checklist (node 105 export) — In-Clinic
        only, gated with the same data-kal-mode-offline-only hook
        applyConsultationModeVisibility() in kal-booking-flow.js already
        toggles for this step's appointment card rows (see that
        function's own comment, which already names this exact card as
        one of the elements it's meant to control). Kept as a sibling of
        .kal-step-booking-confirmed__summary rather than nested inside
        it, so it picks up .kal-step-shell__scroll's own flex gap
        (16px mobile / 24px desktop) below the summary instead of
        needing a margin-top of its own — unlike the hero+card inside
        __summary, there's no overlap here to protect from that gap.
        Same 0 24px side margin as the appointment card above it, with
        its own 750px+ cap matching that card's 608px max-width so both
        stay the same width at every size.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-before-visit" data-kal-mode-offline-only>
        <p class="kal-before-visit__label">Before your visit</p>
        <ul class="kal-before-visit__list">
          <li class="kal-before-visit__item">
            <span class="kal-before-visit__icon">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}</span>
            <span>Pay at reception cash or card.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="kal-before-visit__item">
            <span class="kal-before-visit__icon">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}</span>
            <span>Arrive 10 minutes early for check-in.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="kal-before-visit__item">
            <span class="kal-before-visit__icon">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}</span>
            <span>Bring an ID and your referral letter if you have one.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Video Consult's counterpart to In-Clinic's "Before your visit"
        card above — reuses Therapy Confirmed's own
        .kal-therapy-confirmed-actions/__btn/__icon button treatment
        as-is (same "Shop Products"/"Get directions" pair, no click
        handlers, same decorative-per-this-build's-scope status as
        there) rather than a parallel set of near-duplicate classes.
        Gated with data-kal-mode-online-only, the exact opposite hook
        .kal-before-visit uses, so exactly one of the two ever shows;
        starts `hidden` in markup (same convention as this file's other
        data-kal-mode-online-only elements) so it doesn't flash visible
        before applyConsultationModeVisibility() runs on arrival at this
        step. Sits in the same sibling position .kal-before-visit does,
        below the summary card, with matching 0 24px / 608px-at-750px+
        sizing scoped in CSS rather than duplicated here.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed__online-actions kal-therapy-confirmed-actions" data-kal-mode-online-only hidden>
        <button type="button" class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions__btn">
          <span class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions__icon">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'shopping-cart' -%}
          </span>
          <span>Shop Products</span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions__btn">
          <span class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions__icon">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'directions' -%}
          </span>
          <span>Get directions</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue">Back to Homepage</a>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
